  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mi>mL</mi></math> bottle of soft drink has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>MCO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;dissolved in it. Assuming <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;behaves as an ideal gas, the volume of the dissolved <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at STP is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mL</mi></math>. (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given: At STP, molar volume of an ideal gas is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1362",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Moles dissolved in soft drinks of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>molarity</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>volume</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>300</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>06</mn><mtext>&#160;Mole&#160;</mtext></math></p><p>Volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>06</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mole</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at S.T.P</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>06</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>362</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p>",
